Z||000000||spit||11-12-2001||03:31 PM||||Hello, all.  I have an 86 4cylinder fiero.  It has a problem(go figure).  For a while, when I accelerated, it would rev up and out and up and out etc.  Like this (kinda) VRRRR vr vr vr vr VRRR vrr vr vrr VRRR vrrvrr...<BR>Eventually when I got up to about 40 it would level out.  Then one day when I went to put it in park, it died before I got there.  Now I can get it to start, but it dies after 5-15 seconds.  And when I try to move it to any other gear (it's an automatic) it instantly dies.  <BR>I checked for problems using the code key, but it says nothing is wrong.  I asked a friend/fiero owner who said "I know exactly what the problem is.  It's the throttle positioning sensor."  So I replaced it, and it made absolutely no difference.  Then I asked another friend/mechanic who said it could be any of the idle sensors on the throttle body.  Such as the MAP sensor or the idle air control valve.  So, taking his advice (having nothing to lose), I unplugged each of the sensors and checked the code key with each unplugging.  And started the car with each sensor unplugged.  Nothing happened.  At one point, the code 34 flashed, for the map sensor, but when i unplugged the battery to reset the sensor and tried again, 12 was (and still is) the only code flashing.  <BR>If anyone has any advice or knows what's going on with my car, PLEEASE help.  <BR>OH, and sorry about the length of this thread, I just wanted to get all the facts out.||||reg||1
Z||000001||johnt671||11-12-2001||03:34 PM||||Try the fuel filter if it is old.  Could be a plugged cat. also.||||reg||1
Z||000002||samoht||11-12-2001||05:19 PM||||if it was the filter it would run bad all the time, same with cat..  How does it run with the OBD terminals crossed?  Can you gun it..  Is it only at cruising speed? May be a choke ..  sounds like a fuel prblem..  I would try timing first.  see if you casn get it to even out  What have you replaced recently?<P>85gt3.2||||reg||1
Z||000003||spit||11-13-2001||03:54 AM||||OBD terminals?  What are they?<BR>can I gun it? No, it just dies faster.<BR>Is it only at cruising speed?  Well, no, since it doesnt rev up enough to do anything but die.<BR>What hav I replaced recently?  Well, the spark plugs/wires are the only recent thing.  Actually, I replaced them just before it finally died.  Other than that, it's been several months, but it has a new alternator and belt, anything else was several months before that.<BR>What's a cat?<BR>And i'll find out about the OBD this weekend.  <BR>And thanks for any help.  ||||reg||1
